This crate is a derivative work of the Rust standard library (RCE-D-9 in DESIGN-NOTES.md).

The allocator interface in src/allocator.rs -- the `Allocator` trait with its `allocate` and
`deallocate` methods, `AllocError`, and `Global` -- takes its names and signatures from the
standard library's unstable `core::alloc::Allocator`, `core::alloc::AllocError` and
`alloc::alloc::Global`. The shared error's reference counting follows the standard library's
`alloc::sync::Arc`. The Rust standard library is dual-licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, and the MIT license; it is used here under the MIT license, whose notice follows.

Linux's `kernel::sync::Arc` is credited for the idea of omitting weak references. No code is
taken from it.

